1. Open the Windows Defender Security Center on your laptop or desktop and take a screenshot showing the status of Virus & Threat Protection, Firewall & Network Protection, and App & Browser Control.
==>I opened Windows Security on my Windows computer and checked the
following sections:
● Virus & threat protection
● Firewall & network protection
● App & browser control
Steps
1. Press Windows + I to open Settings.
2. Go to Privacy & security → Windows Security.
3. Select Virus & threat protection and check its status.
4. Go back and select Firewall & network protection.
5. Check the status of the Domain, Private, and Public network firewall.
6. Select App & browser control and check the available protection
settings.


2. Create a new user account on your Windows system and set a strong password that meets at least 3 out of 4 complexity requirements (uppercase, lowercase, number, special character).
=>1. Open Settings.
2. Go to Accounts → Other users.
3. Select Add account.
4. Choose the option to add a user without requiring a Microsoft
account, if a local account is desired.
5. Enter the username.
6. Set a strong password.
7. Complete the account creation process.
Password Requirements
The password should contain at least three of the following four character
types:
● Uppercase letters: A-Z
● Lowercase letters: a-z
● Numbers: 0-9
● Special characters: ! @ # $ %


3. Disable file sharing for the Public folder in Windows and verify that it is no longer accessible from another device on the same network.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Use the 'Advanced sharing settings' in the Network and Sharing Center.</em>
=>Steps
1. Open Control Panel.
2. Select Network and Sharing Center.
3. Select Change advanced sharing settings.
4. Expand the appropriate network profile.
5. Under All Networks, locate Public folder sharing.
6. Select:
○ Turn off Public folder sharing
7. Click Save changes.


4. Configure the Windows Firewall to block all incoming connections for a specific app of your choice (for example, Spotify or Chrome) and test that the app cannot access the internet.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Go to Windows Defender Firewall > Allow an app or feature through Windows Defender Firewall, and adjust the settings.</em>
=>Steps
1. Open Control Panel.
2. Go to System and Security → Windows Defender Firewall.
3. Select Advanced settings.
4. Select Outbound Rules.
5. Click New Rule.
6. Select Program and browse to the application's executable file, such
as Chrome's chrome.exe.
7. Select Block the connection.
8. Apply the rule to the required network profiles.
9. Give the rule a name such as:
○ Block Chrome Internet Access
10. Save the firewall rule.
